<newsitem itemid="470017" id="root" date="1997-03-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Stalexport sets $50 mln convertible bond.</title>
<headline>Stalexport sets $50 mln convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following convertible bond was announced by joint lead managers Flemings and MC-BBL.</p>
<p> BORROWER   STALEXPORT SA</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON     4.50 PCT  MATURITY  **03.APR.02</p>
<p> TYPE  *CONVERTIBLE   ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE  S 03.APR.97</p>
<p> SHARES PER BOND  72.51			  DENOMS (K)  ONE</p>
<p> SALE LIMITS	US/UK/POLAND	    YIELD   8.316 PCT</p>
<p> SPREAD    +150 BP OVER FIVE YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> CONVERSION PERIOD    15.OCT.97-31.MAR.02</p>
<p> REDEMPTION PRICE     122.53 PCT</p>
<p> CONVERSION PRICE     PLN42.459 REPRESENTS APROX 19 PCT PREMIUM</p>
<p>			    OVER FIVE DAY AVERAGE CLOSING SHARE PRICE.</p>
<p> NOTES    *INTO SHARES OF STALEXPORT SA</p>
<p>	    **HARD NON CALL FOR THREE YEARS, THEREAFTER CALLABLE</p>
<p>	    AT ACCRETED VALUE SUBJECT TO 140 PCT TRIGGER.</p>
<p>	    S-SHORT FIRST COUPON 31.DEC.97</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
